.TH FLAMQUENCY 1 "October 2026" "flamquency-sync 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
flamquency \- terminal-based file synchronization with version control
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B flamquency
[\fI\,COMMAND\/\fR] [\fI\,OPTIONS\/\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
FlamQuency-Sync is a terminal-based file synchronization tool with real
version control, snapshots, and one-click rollback. It stores every version
of your files in content-addressable blob storage, can back up to GitHub,
and offers both a Textual TUI and a scriptable CLI.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B sync
Synchronize files according to configuration.
.TP
.B status
Show current sync status.
.TP
.B snapshots
List available snapshots.
.TP
.B rollback
Rollback the whole system to a snapshot.
.TP
.B rollback-file
Rollback a specific file to a chosen version.
.TP
.B diff
Diff two versions of a text file.
.TP
.B watch
Watch directories and auto-sync on changes.
.TP
.B config
Show or edit configuration.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show help and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.flamquency/config.yaml
User configuration.
.TP
.I ~/.flamquency/sync/
Local sync destination.
.TP
.I ~/.flamquency/versions/blobs/
Content-addressable compressed blob storage.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Sync everything:
.B flamquency sync
.TP
Rollback a single config file:
.B flamquency rollback-file ~/.config/hypr/hyprland.conf \-\-version 2
.TP
Launch the TUI:
.B flamquency-tui
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR flamquency-tui (1),
https://github.com/LOSTFlam/FlamQuency-Sync
